gre_applicant(X) & proves_hardship(X) => provides_aid(ets, X). @ "ETS provides financial aid to those GRE applicants who prove economic hardship."
single_parent(X) => proves_hardship(X). @ "Those living in single-parent families or having few resources available to them can prove economic hardship."
few_resources(X) => proves_hardship(X). @ "Those living in single-parent families or having few resources available to them can prove economic hardship."
single_parent(tom). @ "Tom lives in a single-parent family."
few_resources(tom). @ "Tom has few resources available to them."
gre_applicant(tom). @ "Tom is applying to take the GRE test."
? gre_applicant(V) => not provides_aid(ets, V).
